HandoffProbe Dual-Use Disclosure

HandoffProbe is a defensive security testing tool for AI agent handoffs and
cross-protocol agent systems, including A2A and MCP boundaries.

The package contains adversarial test cases and intentionally vulnerable local
fixtures that reproduce security failures involving identity, authorization,
approval scope, credentials, target binding, lifecycle state, replay,
concurrency, audit evidence, context binding, and related handoff behavior.

These capabilities are intended for legitimate security engineering,
development, research, testing, validation, and assessment of systems that the
user owns or is authorized to test.

The bundled vulnerable targets and fixtures exist to provide controlled,
reproducible demonstrations of security failures. They are not intended for
unauthorized access, credential theft, persistence, disruption, evasion,
malware delivery, or testing systems without permission.

Users are responsible for ensuring that their use of HandoffProbe is lawful
and authorized.
